# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Overview {#overview}"
msgstr "Gambaran keseluruhan {#overview}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Rimay augments classical machine learning pipelines with features generated on quantum hardware. The function takes classical tabular data and returns a set of quantum-transformed features. When a quantum system processes the data, it generates rich features that capture nonlinear relationships between the inputs. You can use the generated features on their own, or combined with your original features, to train any classical model. On small- and medium-sized datasets, quantum-transformed features can improve the prediction quality compared to purely classical baselines.\n"
msgstr "Rimay menambah baik saluran paip pembelajaran mesin klasik dengan ciri yang dijana pada perkakasan kuantum. Fungsi ini mengambil data jadual klasik dan mengembalikan set ciri yang diubah secara kuantum. Apabila sistem kuantum memproses data, ia menjana ciri kaya yang menangkap hubungan tak linear antara input. Anda boleh menggunakan ciri yang dijana secara bersendirian, atau digabungkan dengan ciri asal anda, untuk melatih mana-mana model klasik. Pada set data bersaiz kecil dan sederhana, ciri yang diubah secara kuantum boleh meningkatkan kualiti ramalan berbanding garis dasar klasik semata-mata.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This function is built for the following users:\n"
msgstr "Fungsi ini dibina untuk pengguna berikut:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Data science teams with an existing machine learning pipeline on small- and medium-sized tabular datasets, where prediction quality has plateaued. You add Rimay as one additional preprocessing step, without building any quantum circuits yourself.\n"
msgstr "Pasukan sains data yang mempunyai saluran paip pembelajaran mesin sedia ada pada set data jadual bersaiz kecil dan sederhana, di mana kualiti ramalan telah mendatar. Anda menambah Rimay sebagai satu langkah prapemprosesan tambahan, tanpa perlu membina sebarang litar kuantum sendiri.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Researchers who explore quantum methods for machine learning tasks.\n"
msgstr "Penyelidik yang meneroka kaedah kuantum untuk tugas pembelajaran mesin.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Description {#description}"
msgstr "Perihalan {#description}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The quantum feature extraction algorithm [\\[1\\]](#references) combines two principles of quantum machine learning. The first is quantum feature maps, which embed data into a high-dimensional Hilbert space and therefore produce more expressive representations. The second is quantum reservoir computing, which uses the dynamics of a quantum many-body system as a nonlinear transformation of the input.\n"
msgstr "Algoritma pengekstrakan ciri kuantum [\\[1\\]](#references) menggabungkan dua prinsip pembelajaran mesin kuantum. Yang pertama ialah peta ciri kuantum, yang membenamkan data ke dalam ruang Hilbert berdimensi tinggi dan oleh itu menghasilkan perwakilan yang lebih ekspresif. Yang kedua ialah pengkomputeran reservoir kuantum, yang menggunakan dinamik sistem banyak jasad kuantum sebagai transformasi tak linear bagi input.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Rimay encodes the feature values and the mutual information between the features into the local fields and the coupling coefficients of a spin-glass Hamiltonian. Counterdiabatic quantum dynamics evolve the system toward its low-energy states, which contain nonlinear mixtures of the correlations in the input data. Rimay extracts these correlations by measuring single- and two-body expectation values. The expectation values are the quantum-transformed features that you feed into your machine learning model.\n"
msgstr "Rimay mengekod nilai ciri dan maklumat bersama antara ciri ke dalam medan setempat dan pekali gandingan Hamiltonian kaca spin. Dinamik kuantum counterdiabatic mengembangkan sistem ke arah keadaan bertenaga rendahnya, yang mengandungi campuran tak linear bagi korelasi dalam data input. Rimay mengekstrak korelasi ini dengan mengukur nilai jangkaan satu jasad dan dua jasad. Nilai jangkaan ini ialah ciri yang diubah secara kuantum yang anda masukkan ke dalam model pembelajaran mesin anda.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Workflow {#workflow}"
msgstr "Aliran kerja {#workflow}"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Rimay workflow: The training data defines the Hamiltonian, every sample becomes one circuit, and the measured expectation values are returned as quantum-transformed data](/docs/images/guides/kipu-rimay/workflow.svg \"Rimay function workflow\")\n"
msgstr "![Rimay workflow: The training data defines the Hamiltonian, every sample becomes one circuit, and the measured expectation values are returned as quantum-transformed data](/docs/images/guides/kipu-rimay/workflow.svg \"Rimay function workflow\")\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Preprocess your tabular data as you would for classical machine learning. Rimay needs numerical features, so convert categorical features into numerical ones, for example with scikit-learn's [`OneHotEncoder`](https://scikit-learn.org/stable/modules/generated/sklearn.preprocessing.OneHotEncoder.html).\n"
msgstr "Praproses data jadual anda seperti yang anda lakukan untuk pembelajaran mesin klasik. Rimay memerlukan ciri berangka, jadi tukar ciri kategori kepada ciri berangka, contohnya dengan [`OneHotEncoder`](https://scikit-learn.org/stable/modules/generated/sklearn.preprocessing.OneHotEncoder.html) daripada scikit-learn.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Split the data into a training set and a test set, and upload both to the function, as shown in the [Example](#example) section.\n"
msgstr "Pisahkan data kepada set latihan dan set ujian, dan muat naik kedua-duanya ke fungsi, seperti yang ditunjukkan dalam bahagian [Contoh](#example).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Rimay uses the training data to construct the Hamiltonian that represents the data. Every feature corresponds to one qubit, and the full training set decides which features, and therefore which qubits, interact. Rimay stores this structure so that it maps the test data and later inference data with the same Hamiltonian.\n"
msgstr "Rimay menggunakan data latihan untuk membina Hamiltonian yang mewakili data. Setiap ciri sepadan dengan satu qubit, dan keseluruhan set latihan menentukan ciri mana, dan oleh itu qubit mana, yang berinteraksi. Rimay menyimpan struktur ini supaya ia memetakan data ujian dan data inferens kemudian dengan Hamiltonian yang sama.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "For every sample, the feature values set the local fields of the Hamiltonian, and the mutual information between the features sets the coupling coefficients of the structure from step 3. Rimay digitizes the counterdiabatic evolution of this Hamiltonian into a circuit, and runs the circuits on the QPU.\n"
msgstr "Bagi setiap sampel, nilai ciri menetapkan medan setempat Hamiltonian, dan maklumat bersama antara ciri menetapkan pekali gandingan struktur daripada langkah 3. Rimay mendigitalkan evolusi counterdiabatic Hamiltonian ini menjadi litar, dan menjalankan litar tersebut pada QPU.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '5. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Rimay measures the resulting bitstrings, then computes the single-body expectation values and the two-body expectation values of physically coupled qubits.\n"
msgstr "Rimay mengukur rentetan bit yang terhasil, kemudian mengira nilai jangkaan satu jasad dan nilai jangkaan dua jasad bagi qubit yang digandingkan secara fizikal.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '6. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "You download the expectation values in a form that you can feed directly into your model, or combine with your original features.\n"
msgstr "Anda memuat turun nilai jangkaan dalam bentuk yang boleh anda masukkan terus ke dalam model anda, atau gabungkan dengan ciri asal anda.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"Because of this structure, the number of qubits that a run needs equals the number of features, and the number of circuits that it submits equals the number of samples.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"Kerana struktur ini, bilangan qubit yang diperlukan oleh satu larian sama dengan bilangan ciri, dan bilangan litar yang dihantarnya sama dengan bilangan sampel.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "After you fit a mapping, you can map new data through it, for example for inference. Rimay then retrieves the Hamiltonian that it created during the fit and builds the circuits for the new samples from it.\n"
msgstr "Selepas anda memadankan pemetaan, anda boleh memetakan data baharu melaluinya, contohnya untuk inferens. Rimay kemudian mendapatkan semula Hamiltonian yang dicipta semasa pemadanan dan membina litar untuk sampel baharu daripadanya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Integrate Rimay into your machine learning pipeline {#integrate-rimay-into-your-machine-learning-pipeline}"
msgstr "Integrasikan Rimay ke dalam saluran paip pembelajaran mesin anda {#integrate-rimay-into-your-machine-learning-pipeline}"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Pipeline with Rimay inserted between the train-test split and the classical machine learning model](/docs/images/guides/kipu-rimay/pipeline.svg \"Rimay as an additional preprocessing step\")\n"
msgstr "![Pipeline with Rimay inserted between the train-test split and the classical machine learning model](/docs/images/guides/kipu-rimay/pipeline.svg \"Rimay as an additional preprocessing step\")\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "As in a classical pipeline, you start by preprocessing the raw data, for example by one-hot encoding the categorical features, and split it into a training set and a test set. Instead of feeding both sets into your model directly, you feed them into Rimay first, and train your model on the quantum-transformed features.\n"
msgstr "Seperti dalam saluran paip klasik, anda bermula dengan praproses data mentah, contohnya dengan pengekodan one-hot bagi ciri kategori, dan membahagikannya kepada set latihan dan set ujian. Daripada memasukkan kedua-dua set terus ke dalam model anda, anda memasukkannya ke dalam Rimay dahulu, dan melatih model anda pada ciri yang diubah secara kuantum.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Benchmarks {#benchmarks}"
msgstr "Penanda aras {#benchmarks}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Kipu Quantum benchmarked Rimay on the German credit dataset from OpenML [\\[2\\]](#references), which classifies 1000 credit applicants as good or bad credit risks. It has 13 categorical and seven numerical attributes. One-hot encoding of the categorical attributes results in 48 numerical features. The benchmark holds out 20% of the samples as the test set.\n"
msgstr "Kipu Quantum menanda aras Rimay pada set data kredit Jerman daripada OpenML [\\[2\\]](#references), yang mengelaskan 1000 pemohon kredit sebagai risiko kredit baik atau buruk. Ia mempunyai 13 atribut kategori dan tujuh atribut berangka. Pengekodan one-hot bagi atribut kategori menghasilkan 48 ciri berangka. Penanda aras ini mengetepikan 20% sampel sebagai set ujian.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "As a baseline, several classical models were trained on the classical features. With Rimay, a random forest was trained in two ways: on the quantum-transformed features alone (Random forest Q), and on the quantum-transformed features combined with the classical ones (Random forest H, for hybrid). The table reports only the random forest, because it performed best on the quantum-transformed features.\n"
msgstr "Sebagai garis dasar, beberapa model klasik dilatih pada ciri klasik. Dengan Rimay, hutan rawak dilatih dalam dua cara: pada ciri yang diubah secara kuantum sahaja (Random forest Q), dan pada ciri yang diubah secara kuantum digabungkan dengan ciri klasik (Random forest H, untuk hibrid). Jadual hanya melaporkan hutan rawak, kerana ia berprestasi terbaik pada ciri yang diubah secara kuantum.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Model | Features | Accuracy | AUC | F1 score | Precision | Recall |\n"
"| :-- | :-- | --: | --: | --: | --: | --: |\n"
"| [CatBoost](https://catboost.ai/) | Classical | 0.775 | 0.781 | 0.850 | 0.795 | 0.914 |\n"
"| [Random forest](https://scikit-learn.org/stable/modules/generated/sklearn.ensemble.RandomForestClassifier.html) | Classical | 0.765 | 0.781 | 0.846 | 0.782 | 0.921 |\n"
"| [XGBoost](https://xgboost.readthedocs.io/en/stable/) | Classical | 0.760 | 0.758 | 0.835 | 0.803 | 0.871 |\n"
"| [LightGBM](https://lightgbm.readthedocs.io/en/stable/) | Classical | 0.770 | 0.751 | 0.840 | 0.818 | 0.864 |\n"
"| Random forest Q | Quantum | 0.750 | 0.793 | 0.840 | 0.762 | 0.936 |\n"
"| Random forest H | Hybrid | 0.770 | 0.798 | 0.854 | 0.770 | 0.957 |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Model | Ciri | Ketepatan | AUC | Skor F1 | Kepersisan | Dapatan semula |\n"
"| :-- | :-- | --: | --: | --: | --: | --: |\n"
"| [CatBoost](https://catboost.ai/) | Klasik | 0.775 | 0.781 | 0.850 | 0.795 | 0.914 |\n"
"| [Random forest](https://scikit-learn.org/stable/modules/generated/sklearn.ensemble.RandomForestClassifier.html) | Klasik | 0.765 | 0.781 | 0.846 | 0.782 | 0.921 |\n"
"| [XGBoost](https://xgboost.readthedocs.io/en/stable/) | Klasik | 0.760 | 0.758 | 0.835 | 0.803 | 0.871 |\n"
"| [LightGBM](https://lightgbm.readthedocs.io/en/stable/) | Klasik | 0.770 | 0.751 | 0.840 | 0.818 | 0.864 |\n"
"| Random forest Q | Kuantum | 0.750 | 0.793 | 0.840 | 0.762 | 0.936 |\n"
"| Random forest H | Hibrid | 0.770 | 0.798 | 0.854 | 0.770 | 0.957 |\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The hybrid features improve all metrics of the random forest except the precision, and the hybrid random forest reaches a higher AUC, F1 score, and recall than CatBoost on the classical features. The largest effect is on the recall, which rises from 0.921 to 0.957. The quantum-transformed features alone do not reach the precision of the classical models.\n"
msgstr "Ciri hibrid meningkatkan semua metrik hutan rawak kecuali kepersisan, dan hutan rawak hibrid mencapai AUC, skor F1 dan dapatan semula yang lebih tinggi daripada CatBoost pada ciri klasik. Kesan terbesar ialah pada dapatan semula, yang meningkat daripada 0.921 kepada 0.957. Ciri yang diubah secara kuantum sahaja tidak mencapai kepersisan model klasik.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"caution\">\n"
"  The test set holds only 200 samples, so predicting one more sample correctly moves the accuracy by 0.005. Read the differences as a trend that needs further verification, not as a significant effect. The prediction accuracy can also depend on the hardware-induced noise of the extracted features. Therefore, use enough shots that shot noise does not limit the result.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"caution\">\n"
"  Set ujian hanya mengandungi 200 sampel, jadi meramal satu lagi sampel dengan betul mengubah ketepatan sebanyak 0.005. Baca perbezaan ini sebagai trend yang memerlukan pengesahan lanjut, bukan sebagai kesan yang signifikan. Ketepatan ramalan juga boleh bergantung pada hingar akibat perkakasan bagi ciri yang diekstrak. Oleh itu, gunakan bilangan shot yang mencukupi supaya hingar shot tidak menghadkan hasil.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The benchmark used the following resources:\n"
msgstr "Penanda aras menggunakan sumber berikut:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Example | Number of qubits | Number of samples | Number of shots | Total time (min) | QPU usage (min) | Processor |\n"
"| :-- | --: | --: | --: | --: | --: | :-- |\n"
"| German credit | 48 | 1000 | 5000 | 23 | 22 | ibm_boston |\n"
"| German credit | 48 | 1000 | 5000 | 3 |  2 | ibm_phoenix |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Contoh | Bilangan qubit | Bilangan sampel | Bilangan shot | Jumlah masa (min) | Penggunaan QPU (min) | Pemproses |\n"
"| :-- | --: | --: | --: | --: | --: | :-- |\n"
"| German credit | 48 | 1000 | 5000 | 23 | 22 | ibm_boston |\n"
"| German credit | 48 | 1000 | 5000 | 3 |  2 | ibm_phoenix |\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The number of samples, which is the number of circuits, drives the QPU time. Use the Nighthawk r2 processor type, because it greatly reduces the required QPU time.\n"
msgstr "Bilangan sampel, iaitu bilangan litar, menentukan masa QPU. Gunakan jenis pemproses Nighthawk r2, kerana ia sangat mengurangkan masa QPU yang diperlukan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Inputs {#inputs}"
msgstr "Input {#inputs}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The `mode` determines which parameters a run needs. For a description of every input parameter, see the [API reference](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/functions/kipu-rimay#inputs).\n"
msgstr "`mode` menentukan parameter yang diperlukan oleh satu larian. Untuk penerangan setiap parameter input, lihat [rujukan API](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/functions/kipu-rimay#inputs).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Input files {#input-files}"
msgstr "Fail input {#input-files}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Upload every file with `catalog.file_upload()` before you run the function.\n"
msgstr "Muat naik setiap fail dengan `catalog.file_upload()` sebelum anda menjalankan fungsi.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "An upload replaces any earlier file of the same name, even for a job that you submitted but that has not started yet. To run several jobs at the same time, give the files of each job their own names, for example `run1_x_train.csv` and `run2_x_train.csv`.\n"
msgstr "Muat naik menggantikan sebarang fail terdahulu dengan nama yang sama, walaupun untuk tugas yang telah anda serahkan tetapi belum bermula. Untuk menjalankan beberapa tugas pada masa yang sama, berikan fail bagi setiap tugas nama tersendiri, contohnya `run1_x_train.csv` dan `run2_x_train.csv`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Every file is a CSV file with a header row. Every column of a feature file is one feature, and every value must be numeric.\n"
msgstr "Setiap fail ialah fail CSV dengan baris pengepala. Setiap lajur fail ciri ialah satu ciri, dan setiap nilai mestilah berangka.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`y_train` holds exactly one numeric column, with one label per row of `x_train`. Map categorical labels to numbers, for example good and bad to 1 and 0.\n"
msgstr "`y_train` mengandungi tepat satu lajur berangka, dengan satu label bagi setiap baris `x_train`. Petakan label kategori kepada nombor, contohnya baik dan buruk kepada 1 dan 0.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`x_test` and `x_inference` must have the same columns as `x_train`, in the same order.\n"
msgstr "`x_test` dan `x_inference` mestilah mempunyai lajur yang sama dengan `x_train`, dalam susunan yang sama.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"caution\" title=\"Keep the mapping_id and backend_name\">\n"
"  The `mapping_id` is the only way to reach the mapping that your fit produced, and it cannot be looked up or recovered. It authorizes the use of that mapping, so treat it like a credential and do not share it. If you lose it, you must fit a new mapping, which costs another run on quantum hardware. Also record the `backend_name` of the fit, because the mapping runs only on that processor.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"caution\" title=\"Simpan mapping_id dan backend_name\">\n"
"  `mapping_id` ialah satu-satunya cara untuk mencapai pemetaan yang dihasilkan oleh pemadanan anda, dan ia tidak boleh dicari atau dipulihkan. Ia memberi kebenaran untuk menggunakan pemetaan itu, jadi layannya seperti bukti kelayakan dan jangan kongsikannya. Jika anda kehilangannya, anda mesti memadankan pemetaan baharu, yang memerlukan satu lagi larian pada perkakasan kuantum. Rekodkan juga `backend_name` bagi pemadanan itu, kerana pemetaan hanya berjalan pada pemproses tersebut.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Limits {#limits}"
msgstr "Had {#limits}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Every feature is mapped to one qubit, so the processor must have at least as many qubits as your data has features. If you have more features than that, reduce them with a feature selection technique first.\n"
msgstr "Setiap ciri dipetakan kepada satu qubit, jadi pemproses mestilah mempunyai sekurang-kurangnya sebanyak qubit seperti bilangan ciri dalam data anda. Jika anda mempunyai lebih banyak ciri daripada itu, kurangkannya dahulu dengan teknik pemilihan ciri.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Every sample becomes one circuit, and a run counts training and test samples together. A run can hold at most 15,000 samples.\n"
msgstr "Setiap sampel menjadi satu litar, dan satu larian mengira sampel latihan dan ujian bersama-sama. Satu larian boleh mengandungi paling banyak 15,000 sampel.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "A single job can request at most 10 million executions, so the number of samples times `shots` must not exceed 10 million.\n"
msgstr "Satu tugas boleh meminta paling banyak 10 juta pelaksanaan, jadi bilangan sampel darab `shots` tidak boleh melebihi 10 juta.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "A job must finish within 24 hours, including the time its circuits wait in the processor's queue. A job that runs longer is stopped without a result. On a busy processor, keep large datasets well below these limits.\n"
msgstr "Satu tugas mesti selesai dalam masa 24 jam, termasuk masa litarnya menunggu dalam baris gilir pemproses. Tugas yang berjalan lebih lama dihentikan tanpa hasil. Pada pemproses yang sibuk, pastikan set data besar jauh di bawah had ini.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Outputs {#outputs}"
msgstr "Output {#outputs}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`job.result()` returns a dictionary. The quantum-transformed features themselves are written to CSV files that you download with `catalog.file_download()`. For a description of every key of the dictionary, see the [API reference](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/functions/kipu-rimay#output). For the time that each execution phase took, see [Run metadata](#run-metadata).\n"
msgstr "`job.result()` mengembalikan kamus. Ciri yang diubah secara kuantum itu sendiri ditulis ke dalam fail CSV yang anda muat turun dengan `catalog.file_download()`. Untuk penerangan setiap kunci kamus, lihat [rujukan API](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/functions/kipu-rimay#output). Untuk masa yang diambil oleh setiap fasa pelaksanaan, lihat [Metadata larian](#run-metadata).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Every output file holds one row per input row, in the order of the input file, and one column per quantum-transformed feature. The columns whose names start with `corr_` are the two-body expectation values. The files hold no label column. The labels of your training data stay in your `y_train` file.\n"
msgstr "Setiap fail output mengandungi satu baris bagi setiap baris input, mengikut susunan fail input, dan satu lajur bagi setiap ciri yang diubah secara kuantum. Lajur yang namanya bermula dengan `corr_` ialah nilai jangkaan dua jasad. Fail tidak mengandungi lajur label. Label data latihan anda kekal dalam fail `y_train` anda.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Run metadata {#run-metadata}"
msgstr "Metadata larian {#run-metadata}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`resource_usage` holds one entry for each execution phase that the run went through: `\"RUNNING: MAPPING\"`, `\"RUNNING: POST_PROCESSING\"`, and, on a QPU, usually `\"RUNNING: WAITING_FOR_QPU\"`. Each entry holds `CPU_TIME`, the wall-clock time of the phase in seconds, and `QPU_TIME`, the QPU time in seconds. On a QPU, the QPU time that IBM billed is recorded under `\"RUNNING: MAPPING\"`, the phase in which the circuits ran.\n"
msgstr "`resource_usage` mengandungi satu entri bagi setiap fasa pelaksanaan yang dilalui larian: `\"RUNNING: MAPPING\"`, `\"RUNNING: POST_PROCESSING\"`, dan, pada QPU, biasanya `\"RUNNING: WAITING_FOR_QPU\"`. Setiap entri mengandungi `CPU_TIME`, masa jam dinding bagi fasa itu dalam saat, dan `QPU_TIME`, masa QPU dalam saat. Pada QPU, masa QPU yang dibilkan oleh IBM direkodkan di bawah `\"RUNNING: MAPPING\"`, iaitu fasa di mana litar dijalankan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`\"RUNNING: WAITING_FOR_QPU\"` is the time your jobs waited in the IBM queue. The run takes this time from the IBM job timestamps, and does not count it in `\"RUNNING: MAPPING\"`. If IBM does not report those timestamps for every job, the entry is absent, and the wait is part of `\"RUNNING: MAPPING\"`.\n"
msgstr "`\"RUNNING: WAITING_FOR_QPU\"` ialah masa tugas anda menunggu dalam baris gilir IBM. Larian mengambil masa ini daripada cap masa tugas IBM, dan tidak mengiranya dalam `\"RUNNING: MAPPING\"`. Jika IBM tidak melaporkan cap masa tersebut bagi setiap tugas, entri itu tidak wujud, dan masa menunggu menjadi sebahagian daripada `\"RUNNING: MAPPING\"`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "IBM&reg; finishes its usage calculation some time after a job finishes. The run waits up to about a minute for it. Usage that is still being calculated after that time is not included in `QPU_TIME`, and the final usage is shown on IBM Quantum Platform. If the run cannot read the usage from IBM, `QPU_TIME` is `None`.\n"
msgstr "IBM&reg; menyelesaikan pengiraan penggunaannya beberapa ketika selepas tugas selesai. Larian menunggu sehingga kira-kira seminit untuknya. Penggunaan yang masih dikira selepas masa itu tidak disertakan dalam `QPU_TIME`, dan penggunaan akhir dipaparkan di IBM Quantum Platform. Jika larian tidak dapat membaca penggunaan daripada IBM, `QPU_TIME` ialah `None`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For example:\n"
msgstr "Contohnya:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Get started {#get-started}"
msgstr "Bermula {#get-started}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Authenticate using your [IBM Quantum Platform API key](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/), and select the Qiskit Function as follows:\n"
msgstr "Sahkan diri menggunakan [kunci API IBM Quantum Platform](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/) anda, dan pilih Qiskit Function seperti berikut:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"  The following code assumes that you have saved your credentials. If you have not, follow the instructions in [Install the Qiskit Functions Catalog client](/guides/functions-get-started#install-qiskit-functions-catalog-client) to save your account with your API key.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"  Kod berikut menganggap anda telah menyimpan bukti kelayakan anda. Jika belum, ikut arahan dalam [Pasang klien Qiskit Functions Catalog](/guides/functions-get-started#install-qiskit-functions-catalog-client) untuk menyimpan akaun anda dengan kunci API anda.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Function sizes {#function-sizes}"
msgstr "Saiz fungsi {#function-sizes}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Every job runs at one size — `S`, `M`, or `L`. If the specified size is too small, the job is rejected. If the size is larger than needed, it runs on a bigger compute profile than the work requires.\n"
msgstr "Setiap tugas berjalan pada satu saiz — `S`, `M`, atau `L`. Jika saiz yang ditentukan terlalu kecil, tugas ditolak. Jika saiz lebih besar daripada yang diperlukan, tugas berjalan pada profil pengiraan yang lebih besar daripada yang diperlukan oleh kerja itu.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The size of a Rimay job depends on the number of samples it maps: the rows of `x_train` and `x_test` for `fit-transform`, and the rows of `x_inference` for `transform`. The labels in `y_train` do not count, and a `delete` run maps no samples.\n"
msgstr "Saiz tugas Rimay bergantung pada bilangan sampel yang dipetakannya: baris `x_train` dan `x_test` untuk `fit-transform`, dan baris `x_inference` untuk `transform`. Label dalam `y_train` tidak dikira, dan larian `delete` tidak memetakan sebarang sampel.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Size | Samples per job | Compute profile | vCPU | RAM |\n"
"| :-- | :-- | :-- | :-- | :-- |\n"
"| `S` | Up to 2,999 | `8x32` | 8 | 32 GB |\n"
"| `M` | 3,000 to 9,999 | `8x32` | 8 | 32 GB |\n"
"| `L` | 10,000 to 15,000 | `16x128` | 16 | 128 GB |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Saiz | Sampel setiap tugas | Profil pengiraan | vCPU | RAM |\n"
"| :-- | :-- | :-- | :-- | :-- |\n"
"| `S` | Sehingga 2,999 | `8x32` | 8 | 32 GB |\n"
"| `M` | 3,000 hingga 9,999 | `8x32` | 8 | 32 GB |\n"
"| `L` | 10,000 hingga 15,000 | `16x128` | 16 | 128 GB |\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The number of samples is the only criterion. A size changes nothing but the compute profile: the [limits](#limits) on features, samples, and shots are the same for every size. `S` and `M` run on the same compute profile and differ in the number of samples each covers.\n"
msgstr "Bilangan sampel ialah satu-satunya kriteria. Saiz tidak mengubah apa-apa selain profil pengiraan: [had](#limits) bagi ciri, sampel dan shot adalah sama untuk setiap saiz. `S` dan `M` berjalan pada profil pengiraan yang sama dan berbeza pada bilangan sampel yang dilindungi oleh setiap satu.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The default is `M`, used when a job does not request a size. A job of more than 9,999 samples must therefore request `L`.\n"
msgstr "Lalai ialah `M`, digunakan apabila tugas tidak meminta saiz. Oleh itu, tugas dengan lebih daripada 9,999 sampel mesti meminta `L`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "You can also read the mapping off the function itself with `rimay.sizes_map`, and the size that a job runs at when it does not request one with `rimay.default_size`.\n"
msgstr "Anda juga boleh membaca pemetaan itu daripada fungsi itu sendiri dengan `rimay.sizes_map`, dan saiz yang digunakan oleh tugas apabila ia tidak meminta satu saiz dengan `rimay.default_size`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Calculate the size before submitting {#calculate-the-size-before-submitting}"
msgstr "Kira saiz sebelum menyerahkan {#calculate-the-size-before-submitting}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Run this on your own inputs. It reads them and does nothing else: no job is submitted and nothing is reserved, so you can call it as often as you like.\n"
msgstr "Jalankan ini pada input anda sendiri. Ia membacanya dan tidak melakukan apa-apa lagi: tiada tugas diserahkan dan tiada apa yang ditempah, jadi anda boleh memanggilnya sebanyak yang anda suka.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Pass the data sets themselves, not their file names, in the same order as `input_file`, together with the `mode` of the run. [Step 2 of the example](#2-run-the-function) shows the call.\n"
msgstr "Hantar set data itu sendiri, bukan nama failnya, dalam susunan yang sama dengan `input_file`, bersama `mode` larian. [Langkah 2 contoh](#2-run-the-function) menunjukkan panggilan tersebut.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If the size is too small, the job fails with error `4600` and the message names the size to use instead. If it is larger than needed, the job runs normally and records a `4601` advisory event.\n"
msgstr "Jika saiz terlalu kecil, tugas gagal dengan ralat `4600` dan mesej itu menamakan saiz yang perlu digunakan. Jika ia lebih besar daripada yang diperlukan, tugas berjalan seperti biasa dan merekodkan peristiwa nasihat `4601`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Example {#example}"
msgstr "Contoh {#example}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This example shows how to upload data, run the function, and retrieve the quantum-transformed features. For an end-to-end example that includes the preprocessing and the training of the classical model, see the [tutorial](/tutorials/classify-credit-risk-with-rimay-quantum-feature-extraction).\n"
msgstr "Contoh ini menunjukkan cara memuat naik data, menjalankan fungsi, dan mendapatkan semula ciri yang diubah secara kuantum. Untuk contoh hujung ke hujung yang merangkumi praproses dan latihan model klasik, lihat [tutorial](/tutorials/classify-credit-risk-with-rimay-quantum-feature-extraction).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "1. Upload the data {#1-upload-the-data}"
msgstr "1. Muat naik data {#1-upload-the-data}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This example uses a small synthetic dataset with four numeric features and a binary label, so that a run needs only four qubits and finishes quickly. The next cell writes it to four CSV files: the training features, the training labels, the test features, and the features for step 4 of this example. To use your own data, write your preprocessed training and test sets to files with the same layout instead.\n"
msgstr "Contoh ini menggunakan set data sintetik kecil dengan empat ciri berangka dan satu label binari, supaya satu larian hanya memerlukan empat qubit dan selesai dengan cepat. Sel seterusnya menulisnya ke empat fail CSV: ciri latihan, label latihan, ciri ujian, dan ciri untuk langkah 4 contoh ini. Untuk menggunakan data anda sendiri, tulis set latihan dan ujian anda yang telah diproses ke dalam fail dengan susun atur yang sama.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Upload the training and test files. You upload `x_inference.csv` in step 4.\n"
msgstr "Muat naik fail latihan dan ujian. Anda memuat naik `x_inference.csv` dalam langkah 4.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "2. Run the function {#2-run-the-function}"
msgstr "2. Jalankan fungsi {#2-run-the-function}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Calculate the size of the run from the data that you uploaded, with the calculator from [Function sizes](#calculate-the-size-before-submitting).\n"
msgstr "Kira saiz larian daripada data yang anda muat naik, dengan kalkulator daripada [Saiz fungsi](#calculate-the-size-before-submitting).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Select a processor with at least as many qubits as your data has features, and run the function in `fit-transform` mode with that size. The sample data has four features, so any IBM Quantum processor can run it.\n"
msgstr "Pilih pemproses dengan sekurang-kurangnya sebanyak qubit seperti bilangan ciri dalam data anda, dan jalankan fungsi dalam mod `fit-transform` dengan saiz itu. Data sampel mempunyai empat ciri, jadi mana-mana pemproses IBM Quantum boleh menjalankannya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Check the workload's [status](/guides/functions-get-started#check-job-status) or return [results](/guides/functions-get-started#retrieve-results) as follows:\n"
msgstr "Semak [status](/guides/functions-get-started#check-job-status) beban kerja atau kembalikan [hasil](/guides/functions-get-started#retrieve-results) seperti berikut:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "3. Retrieve the results {#3-retrieve-the-results}"
msgstr "3. Dapatkan semula hasil {#3-retrieve-the-results}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Download the quantum-transformed features. Pass `target_name` so that each file is saved under its own name.\n"
msgstr "Muat turun ciri yang diubah secara kuantum. Hantar `target_name` supaya setiap fail disimpan di bawah namanya sendiri.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "4. Map new data {#4-map-new-data}"
msgstr "4. Petakan data baharu {#4-map-new-data}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "After you train your model, map new data with the fitted mapping, for example to run inference. This example maps `x_inference.csv`, which the first cell of this example wrote. Pass the `mapping_id` that the fit returned, so that the new rows are mapped with the same mapping instead of a new one.\n"
msgstr "Selepas anda melatih model anda, petakan data baharu dengan pemetaan yang telah dipadankan, contohnya untuk menjalankan inferens. Contoh ini memetakan `x_inference.csv`, yang ditulis oleh sel pertama contoh ini. Hantar `mapping_id` yang dikembalikan oleh pemadanan, supaya baris baharu dipetakan dengan pemetaan yang sama dan bukan yang baharu.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A mapping is built for the qubit layout of one processor, so pass the same `backend_name` as the fit, which the fit returned in `result[\"backend_name\"]`. Do not use `least_busy()` to choose the processor, because it might return a different one. Rimay rejects any other processor before it submits anything. The shot count also comes from the fit.\n"
msgstr "Pemetaan dibina untuk susun atur qubit satu pemproses, jadi hantar `backend_name` yang sama dengan pemadanan, yang dikembalikan oleh pemadanan dalam `result[\"backend_name\"]`. Jangan gunakan `least_busy()` untuk memilih pemproses, kerana ia mungkin mengembalikan yang lain. Rimay menolak mana-mana pemproses lain sebelum ia menyerahkan apa-apa. Bilangan shot juga datang daripada pemadanan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "5. Delete a mapping {#5-delete-a-mapping}"
msgstr "5. Padam pemetaan {#5-delete-a-mapping}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "When you no longer need a fitted mapping, delete it. A `delete` run does no quantum work, so it needs no processor, no shots, and no function size. You cannot undo a deletion. After deletion, the `mapping_id` no longer refers to anything, and a `transform` run with it fails.\n"
msgstr "Apabila anda tidak lagi memerlukan pemetaan yang telah dipadankan, padamkannya. Larian `delete` tidak melakukan kerja kuantum, jadi ia tidak memerlukan pemproses, shot, atau saiz fungsi. Anda tidak boleh membuat asal pemadaman. Selepas pemadaman, `mapping_id` tidak lagi merujuk kepada apa-apa, dan larian `transform` dengannya gagal.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Fetch error messages {#fetch-error-messages}"
msgstr "Dapatkan mesej ralat {#fetch-error-messages}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If your workload status is `ERROR`, use `job.error_message()` to fetch the error message, as follows:\n"
msgstr "Jika status beban kerja anda ialah `ERROR`, gunakan `job.error_message()` untuk mendapatkan mesej ralat, seperti berikut:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Every error that Rimay reports carries a code from the [IBM Quantum error codes](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/errors), a message, and a solution that names the value that you passed and the value that is allowed. The following table lists the most common errors:\n"
msgstr "Setiap ralat yang dilaporkan oleh Rimay membawa kod daripada [kod ralat IBM Quantum](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/errors), satu mesej, dan satu penyelesaian yang menamakan nilai yang anda hantar dan nilai yang dibenarkan. Jadual berikut menyenaraikan ralat yang paling lazim:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Code | Cause |\n"
"| :-- | :-- |\n"
"| `1221` | A parameter is missing or has the wrong type, `mode` is not valid, a file named in `input_file` was not uploaded, the files do not match each other, a feature is not numeric, or the `mapping_id` does not match a stored mapping. |\n"
"| `1221` | A `\"transform\"` run names a different `backend_name` than the fit that produced its mapping. |\n"
"| `1216` | Your instance has no processor with the `backend_name` that you passed. The solution lists the processors it does have. |\n"
"| `1200` | Your API key does not have access to the instance that the job runs under. |\n"
"| `3200` | `backend_name` does not start with `ibm_`. |\n"
"| `4500` | The data has more features than the processor has qubits. |\n"
"| `6000` | The number of samples times `shots` exceeds 10 million executions. |\n"
"| `6001` | `shots` is smaller than 1. |\n"
"| `6002` | The data has more samples than a run allows. |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Kod | Punca |\n"
"| :-- | :-- |\n"
"| `1221` | Parameter tiada atau mempunyai jenis yang salah, `mode` tidak sah, fail yang dinamakan dalam `input_file` tidak dimuat naik, fail tidak sepadan antara satu sama lain, ciri bukan berangka, atau `mapping_id` tidak sepadan dengan pemetaan yang disimpan. |\n"
"| `1221` | Larian `\"transform\"` menamakan `backend_name` yang berbeza daripada pemadanan yang menghasilkan pemetaannya. |\n"
"| `1216` | Instans anda tidak mempunyai pemproses dengan `backend_name` yang anda hantar. Penyelesaian menyenaraikan pemproses yang dimilikinya. |\n"
"| `1200` | Kunci API anda tidak mempunyai akses kepada instans di bawah mana tugas berjalan. |\n"
"| `3200` | `backend_name` tidak bermula dengan `ibm_`. |\n"
"| `4500` | Data mempunyai lebih banyak ciri daripada bilangan qubit pemproses. |\n"
"| `6000` | Bilangan sampel darab `shots` melebihi 10 juta pelaksanaan. |\n"
"| `6001` | `shots` lebih kecil daripada 1. |\n"
"| `6002` | Data mempunyai lebih banyak sampel daripada yang dibenarkan oleh satu larian. |\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use cases {#use-cases}"
msgstr "Kes penggunaan {#use-cases}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In tabular classification on small- and medium-sized datasets, Kipu Quantum has applied quantum feature extraction to the following:\n"
msgstr "Dalam pengelasan berjadual pada set data bersaiz kecil dan sederhana, Kipu Quantum telah menggunakan pengekstrakan ciri kuantum untuk perkara berikut:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "[Credit risk classification](https://www.openml.org/search?type=data&sort=runs&id=31&status=active)\n"
msgstr "[Pengelasan risiko kredit](https://www.openml.org/search?type=data&sort=runs&id=31&status=active)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "[Molecular toxicity classification](https://arxiv.org/abs/2510.13807)\n"
msgstr "[Pengelasan ketoksikan molekul](https://arxiv.org/abs/2510.13807)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Beyond tabular data, frozen neural networks can transform images into numerical features, which quantum feature extraction then maps into quantum-transformed features:\n"
msgstr "Selain data berjadual, rangkaian neural beku boleh mengubah imej kepada ciri berangka, yang kemudian dipetakan oleh pengekstrakan ciri kuantum kepada ciri yang diubah secara kuantum:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
